 "kind": "definition",
 "title": "Open-immersion square",
 "statement": "An *open-immersion square* is a pair consisting of a\ncartesian square\n\n$$\n\\begin{array}{ccc}\nU'&\\xrightarrow{g_U}&U\\\\\nj'\\downarrow&&\\downarrow j\\\\\nX'&\\xrightarrow{g}&X\n\\end{array}\n$$\n\nin which $j:U\\hookrightarrow X$ and $j':U'\\hookrightarrow X'$ are\nopen immersions, so that\n$U'=U\\times_XX'$; no hypothesis on $g$ is made.",
 "source": {
